  el(h,method,'p','','Each sampled map combines its kills as 1 − product((1 − per-kill chance)^kill count). These conditional probabilities are averaged, so rare drops remain measurable without waiting for lucky loot rolls. Expected runs = 1 / mean run chance; the 50%/90% figures use independent fresh runs. The middle 80% is variation between sampled maps, not a confidence interval for the model. Seed controls reproducibility; more samples reduce sampling noise, not map-model uncertainty.');
